tellraw @a {"text": "Exploded relief: zodiac dial, gear train, crank and pointer.", "color": "white"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Hellenistic Greece, c. 150-60 BCE", "color": "yellow"}
tellraw @a {"text": "A hand-cranked bronze geared calculator that displayed the positions of the Sun, Moon and", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "probably the five planets, the Moon's phase, eclipse predictions (Saros cycle) and the", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "dates of the Olympic Games. At least 30 bronze gears survive.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Turning a crank advances a 365-day calendar dial; gear trains with precise tooth counts", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "reproduce astronomical ratios, including a pin-and-slot device that models the Moon's", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "varying speed (its anomaly). The back dials spiral through the 19-year Metonic and", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "223-month Saros cycles.", "color": "gray"}
